# Deploy

These pages are for an operator running the server for others over HTTP, as a container or a system service, with every caller authenticated. Each page covers one task.

- [Docker](docker.md): the image, Compose, ports, volumes and health checks.
- [Authentication](authentication.md): bearer tokens or OIDC, and when to use which.
- [OIDC](oidc.md): the two OIDC modes, the identity provider's side, and running under a path prefix behind a proxy.
{% if enable_authorization %}- [Authorization](authorization.md): gating individual tools by scope, once callers are authenticated.
{% endif %}
Before exposing the server, read the [security model](../security-model.md): an authenticated caller has every tool the instance exposes, and under OIDC the identity provider alone decides who gets in.

